# Frontend Motion & Animation

## Default stack

**Motion** (`motion`, formerly Framer Motion) is the default library for UI motion—use it for layout transitions, gestures, and enter/exit unless a lighter CSS-only transition is enough.

**Also use:**

- **Tailwind**: `transition-[colors,opacity,…]`, `duration-200`, `ease-out`.
- **`motion-safe:`** / **`motion-reduce:`** (and `motion-reduce:animate-none`).
- **CSS** `@keyframes` when Motion is unnecessary.

Do **not** add **GSAP**, **React Three Fiber**, **Rive**, or **Lottie/dotLottie** unless the user explicitly asks for that stack.

## Heavy libraries (only when requested)

| Need | Library |
|------|---------|
| Timelines, ScrollTrigger, SVG morph | GSAP |
| WebGL / 3D | React Three Fiber |
| Designer-export loops | Lottie / dotLottie |
| Stateful vector mascots | Rive |

## Performance

- Prefer **transform** and **opacity** over layout properties (`width`, `height`, `top`, `margin`).
- Avoid **`transition-all`**—list properties explicitly.
- Use **`will-change` sparingly** and only during active animation.
- Respect **`prefers-reduced-motion`**.
- Lazy-load heavy animation modules/routes.

## Design

- Motion supports hierarchy and feedback; it should not obstruct readability or contrast (see `frontend-styling.mdc`).
- Glassmorphism / heavy gradients only when they aid comprehension—not as default chrome.
